# Demo clips (assets/recordings/<name>.mp4) are Git LFS.
#
# Unanchored on purpose. The previous rule, `assets/recordings/**/*.mp4`,
# silently matched nothing: a gitattributes pattern containing a slash is
# anchored to the .gitattributes directory, so it only ever covered a repo-root
# `assets/recordings/`, never `templates/<name>/assets/recordings/`. Verified
# with `git check-attr`. It looked correct for as long as no clip existed.
#
# LFS matters here because installing a template downloads a zip of this whole
# repo from codeload, and that archive carries LFS pointers rather than the
# bytes. Committing clips as plain objects would put every template's video into
# every install of every other template.
#
# Note for whoever wires clips into the catalog gallery: build their URLs
# against media.githubusercontent.com/media/..., NOT raw.githubusercontent.com.
# The raw host returns the LFS pointer file as the body; the media host returns
# the real bytes.
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
